<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The deportation of the people of Judah to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar II in the early sixth century BC — in waves around 597 and 587/586 BC, with the burning of Jerusalem and Solomon's Temple — until Cyrus of Persia allowed exiles to return in 538 BC; the crisis that reshaped Israel's faith and much of the Old Testament." .
