<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How does Luke describe his purpose in Luke 1:1-4, and what does that tell you about the kind of book he is writing?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Revelation 1:1-4 calls the book a revelation, a prophecy and (by its greeting) a letter. How might each of these shape the way you read it?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which part of the Bible do you find hardest to read, and could knowing more about its kind of writing help?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#after> "These are proverbs, not laws. Placed side by side, they teach that sometimes silence is wise and sometimes a reply is needed, and wisdom lies in discerning which situation I am in." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#before> "Verse 4 says don't answer a fool and verse 5 says answer him, so one of these must be wrong, and Proverbs can't be trusted." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#situation> "A small-group member reads Proverbs 26:4 and 26:5 side by side and concludes that the Bible contradicts itself." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#why> "Proverbs are short sayings that capture general truths for particular situations; reading them as rigid rules or guarantees misses how the genre works." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before interpreting a passage, ask what kind of writing it is (narrative, law, poetry, proverb, prophecy, gospel, letter or apocalypse) and look for clues the book gives about itself." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Note the features of that kind of writing, such as parallel lines and imagery in poetry, short general sayings in proverbs, or greetings and arguments in letters." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask what that kind of writing is designed to do (tell what happened, command, praise, give practical wisdom, warn, comfort or encourage endurance) and let that purpose guide your conclusions." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Compare passages where the Bible tells the same thing in two forms, such as the Red Sea in Exodus 14 and 15, and notice what each form adds." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Check your genre judgment with a study Bible or Bible dictionary, and hold it humbly where careful readers disagree." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Apply the passage in a way that fits its genre, taking a promise as a promise, a proverb as wise counsel and a song as praise to join." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Genre in the Bible" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/1> .
