<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "According to Jeremiah 29:1-10, who first received the letter containing verse 11, where were they, and how long did God say they would wait?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read Philippians 4:10-14. What \"all things\" is Paul talking about in verse 13, and how does that change the way the verse is often used?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Revelation 3:20 is often used in evangelism. To whom is it first addressed (Revelation 3:14-22), and what does that add to its meaning?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which verse do you hold dear but have never read in its surrounding chapter, and what do you notice when you read the whole chapter this week?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#after> "God told exiles in Babylon to settle in and seek the city's peace, promising a future after seventy years; I can trust his good purposes and be faithful where I am, even if this interview fails." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#before> "God has promised me success and no setbacks, so this interview is bound to work out." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#situation> "A friend facing a job interview posts Jeremiah 29:11 as a guarantee that everything will go well." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#why> "Reading the whole letter (Jeremiah 29:1-14) shows a promise of long-range hope to a community in exile, which still comforts believers today but not as a pledge of quick personal success." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Read the whole paragraph, and then the whole chapter, around the verse before deciding what it means." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask who is speaking, to whom, and in what situation; note what the book itself tells you about its author and first readers." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Trace the flow of thought by asking what comes just before, what comes just after, and how the verse fits the argument or story." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Identify the kind of writing (letter, poem, prophecy, narrative) and read it the way that kind of writing is meant to be read." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Use a study Bible or Bible dictionary to fill in historical and cultural background, without letting the background drown out the text." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Compare the passage with other Scripture on the same subject, especially clearer passages, and see how it fits the whole story that centres on Christ." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7> <https://schema.org/position> "7"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7> <https://schema.org/text> "Only then ask what the passage means for you or your church, applying it in a way its first readers would recognise as faithful to it." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Reading in Context" .
